Good read.<BR>It pretty much sums up my impressions of DAoC.<P>Of course there are some down sides but no game is perfect.<P>Here's an example of game play:<BR>Kruunk,<BR>Verser,<BR>Foggy,<BR>Kruikan,<BR>Mig,<BR>Ette,<BR>Baisher.<P>2 tanks, 1 healer, 1 rogue and 3 casters.<P>We are killing blues & yellows (even and under cons)<BR>For 2 hours straight all we did was pull and kill.  Verser OUR ONLY healer for rest of the group was busy but NEVER ran so low on mana that we were in danger.  We were pulling so fast and things were dying so fast that in 2 hours we had all COMPLETELY filled our backpacks full of yummy loot.  We looted 2 RARE items from low level mobs.  One of these items is AWESOME for a caster of our level.  The BEST part was that we all got decent exp, even the 2 members of the group that were only 8th level.  The rest of the group was 10+.  We had 2 deaths (the same guy) from the lower level players but Verser just rezzed them ... YES at 10th level you get REZ!!!  Game play continued and we kept killing and looting and having a blast .. it was a total slaughter fest!!!<P>Do that in EQ with just 1 group.<P>Also after being to the Hole raid with OSW I have one more GREAT thing about DAoC.  In EQ there is only one group or person that get's exp from a kill.  In DAoC anyone that participated in the fight, EVEN outside the group, gets EXP!!!!<P>--------------------<P> <img src="http://people.mn.mediaone.net/raven13/images/Ghall.gif"> 
