<I>In DAoC anyone that participated in the fight, EVEN outside the group, gets EXP!!!!</I><P>That is one of the big changes from MUDs to EQ.  In many MUDs you got experience for each hit on the mob, so by the time the mob died, its total experience had already been dished out piecemeal to everyone attacking it.  That system really works well for 100% hack-n-slash (higher level people do more damage, so they gain more experience, but they also need more exp to level)  It works out very fairly.  I realize EQ had to change that in order to account for classes like clerics, for instance, that might go for hours without inflicting any direct damage to a mob.  I wonder how exp is calculated in DAoC, could someone just hang out by a big group and leech experience from them?  Can 100 people get exp from a kill, and would it just be 1/100 of the total exp?
