From within a group it's a split percentage based on persons in the group and EXP caps of each of those persons.  Outside the group it's damage done .. you get no exp for healing someone that is attacking an NPC.<P>If someone was attacking an NPC and they die and you finish it off .. you only get a percentage of it's exp based on the HP's remaining.  That exp is distributed to the group evenly, excluding exp caps.<P>Each level has a max amount of exp you can get from an NPC so that you can really PL a player beyond what they might achieve ina group of people their own level.  It is a little faster to group with HL people but not so much so that it's unbalancing.<P>You get a group exp bonus based on the number of people in your group .. that exp bonus is shown to you each time you kill an NPC.<P>Yes someone outside your group can leech exp from you by attacking something you are attacking, but the game was kinda designed with that in mind.<P>When you are given a task to kill a creature, as long as you damage a creature of that type .. your task will be accomplished.  If 5 people need a quest item from an NPC and they are all grouped they will ALL get the item .. I'm not sure what happens if you are not in the group.<P>--------------------<P> <img src="http://people.mn.mediaone.net/raven13/images/Ghall.gif"> 
