Getting back to the original topic of this post, I did go out and buy DAoC last night (you bastards)<P>So far I've been unimpressed with the game (played for about 3 hours so far).  The next revision to EQ could easily match everything that this game has going for it.  DAoC might as well be the entire EverQuest engine running intact with someone else's graphics in place, and a few of the keys in a different location.  Its the exact same game.  Its new and different, but not anymore so then a new continent or world would be in EQ.<P>The interfaces are cumbersome and crowded.  If you're in a group of 3-5 people, you spend as much time scrolling back to read everyone's group chat as you do anything else (you only get 4 lines of text for chat, and the font is HUGE, so if three people each say something and one of those lines was more then 30-40 characters long you'll have to scroll back to read it all)  I sure hope you can change the font size.<P>Anyway, I'll give the game more of a chance before passing final judgement, but so far I haven't seen anything truly unique about this game to set it apart from EQ.<P>I've created a Troll Viking on Midgard.  Any preference for an Alpha Group character?  I certainly don't have my heart set on anything yet, so if we're in need of any class, I can play it.
